obtained for laboratory HPV studies. C. R. Key supported the development of the Tissue Acquisition Section (TAS), which identified and ascertained all case materials. W. G. V. Quint conducted blinded SPF-based laboratory analyses. P. E. Castle prepared the initial manuscript draft and participated in critical study analyses. All authors provided critical input to the analyses and manuscript drafting process and approved the final manuscript submitted.</p></fn><fn><p>The authors would like to thank the clinic staff at University of New Mexico Hospital (UNMH) and Lovelace women's health clinics; the statewide pathology laboratories (ie, UNMH, Presbyterian Hospital, Tricore Laboratories, Lovelace Hospital, St Joseph's Hospital, SED Laboratories, Pathology Consultants of New Mexico, St Vincent's Hospital, Las Cruces Memorial Hospital, Las Cruces Mountain View Hospital, San Juan Regional Medical Center, Rehoboth McKinley Hospital, Gila Regional Medical Center, Leah Regional Medical Center, and Taos Holy Cross Hospital) that provided slides and tissue blocks to the study; the project TAS study staff, Lori Lambert, MS, and Rosalina S. Hundley, MS; the study coordinators for this project; and Meifen F. Zhao, MD, MS, Cheri L. Peyton, MS, and J.-P. Brunsveld, who performed the HPV laboratory assays.</p></fn><fn><p>Roche Molecular Systems provided the HPV line blot PCR assay reagents for this project. No potential conflicts of interest are reported by W. C. Hunt, N. Joste, C. Key, and P. E. Castle.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>